# Layer 1 — product factory for {{ project.name }}

This turns the project into a **self-modifying product**: a non-technical user
("builder") describes changes in plain language and the factory ships them.

```
builder (browser chat :8080)
  -> builder/server.py  (spawns `claude -p`)
     -> builder-orchestrator agent  (plain language)
        -> Layer 0 factory (planner/developer/reviewer/test-validator/merger)
           -> verify gate -> definition-of-done
  -> plain-language reply: "I added ... to your app"
```

## Run

```bash
export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...      # or a Claude Code subscription login
docker compose up --build
# open http://localhost:8080
```

Everything runs **inside the container**, which is why the factory can use
`--dangerously-skip-permissions` — the builder never needs to approve technical
prompts, and the agent has no access outside the sandbox.

## Security model (read before exposing this anywhere)

This server drives an **unsandboxed** agent over the mounted repo. It is hardened
for *local single-user* use, not for the open internet:

- **Loopback only.** `docker-compose.yml` maps `127.0.0.1:8080:8080` — never the
  LAN. Do not change it to `0.0.0.0`.
- **Token-gated.** `/chat` requires the `X-Builder-Token` header. Set
  `BUILDER_TOKEN` to a fixed value, or let the server mint a random one at
  startup (printed to the log; the bundled chat page is pre-authorized).
- **Host-checked.** Requests with a non-loopback `Host` are rejected (403), which
  defeats DNS-rebinding from a browser tab you happen to have open.
- **Single-flight.** One build at a time; a second concurrent request gets a
  "busy" reply instead of racing `claude` on one git index.

To put this in front of more than one trusted user, add real auth (reverse proxy
+ SSO), run each request on an isolated worktree, and require human review before
promoting to the live branch.

## Pieces

- `builder/server.py` — stdlib chat server; each message runs the factory once.
- `builder/index.html` — the chat UI.
- `.claude/agents/builder-orchestrator.md` — the user-facing orchestrator
  (plain language; drives the Layer 0 team).
- `Dockerfile` / `docker-compose.yml` — isolation + runtime.
- `deploy/deploy.sh` — gated deploy to {{ delivery.deploy_target }}.

## Hardening before real use

- The built-in token is single-user; add real multi-user auth (reverse proxy + SSO).
- Run each request on an isolated git worktree/branch; review before promoting to
  the live branch.
- Keep secrets in env/secret store; never in the image or the repo.
- Put the app behind the same container; expose only what's needed.
